  "live_records": {
    "q-131165": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131165",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12(x-1)}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{12(x-1)}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{12}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{x}+\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =6-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
