    "q-90533": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90533",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{2},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{40}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
