    "q-131259": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131259",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈0.6931,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+4}{24}, & -4<x<2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 2\\le x<4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x+4}{24}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{\\int }_{-4}^{2}({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{-4}^{2}+x{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{18}+\\frac{8}{9}+2 \\\\  & =3.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈3.5-(0.6931)^{2} \\\\  & ≈3.02.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
