    "q-90566": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90566",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{6},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{27}, & 0<x<3, \\\\ \\frac{9}{{x}^{4}}, & 3\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{27}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{27}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{81}|}_{0}^{3}+{(-\\frac{9}{x})|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{3}-{(\\frac{11}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{83}{36} \\\\  & ≈2.31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
