    "q-90542": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90542",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.238\\,10,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}, & 1\\le x<2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{35}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ≈1.882\\,54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈1.882\\,54-(1.238\\,10)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
