    "q-131260": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131260",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{10(x-1)}{{x}^{6}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{10(x-1)}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10x-10}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}){|}_{0}^{1}+(-\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{10}{3{x}^{3}}){|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}+0+5-\\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-131260-a",
